  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe browser build now loads the user's own machine (`.mch`) and post (`.cps`) files. The bytes come from the browser, not from a path.\n\n- **Load machine (.mch)** and **Load post (.cps)** are live in the browser. They open the browser file picker. A picked machine is mounted. A picked post is selected.\n- The Machine page has a new button **Load folder (.mch, .cps)** in the browser build only. It opens `<input webkitdirectory multiple>`. It adds each `.mch` and `.cps` file of the folder to the session lists. It does not need the File System Access API.\n- A drop with a `.mch` or `.cps` file goes to a new module `setup_file_drop`. One file is mounted or selected. Several files only join the lists. One status line counts the files that landed and names each refused file with its reason.\n- On the desktop, one dropped `.mch` or `.cps` on disk goes to `LoadMachineFile` or `SelectPostFile` by its full path.\n- A new app module `session_files` keeps each file by its bare name for the session, on the thread that loaded it. A file enters it only when it passes the checks of a file from disk: a machine must validate and parse, a post must compile and run.\n- The readers of machine and post files consult the session store first, then the disk. So `LoadMachineFile`, `SelectPostFile` and the MCP tools run unchanged. Each mount and post choice stays one undo step.\n- Session machines show in the machine catalogue (`library::enumerate`). Session posts show in the post combo list.\n- A saved project that names a session file which is not loaded again is refused by that name (#2319). There is no fallback.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe browser build had no disk and no picker for these files. `browser_files::refusal` greyed Load machine and Load post with `NEEDS_PICKER`. The file drop took model files only. The readers of `PostRef::File` and the machine file read only from disk.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/browser_setup_files.rs`:\n\n- `a_dropped_mch_mounts_by_its_name_and_one_undo_takes_it_away`\n- `a_dropped_cps_is_selected_and_posts_from_its_bytes`\n- `several_dropped_files_land_and_each_bad_one_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_malformed_pick_is_refused_by_name_and_changes_nothing`\n- `a_picked_folder_fills_both_lists_and_a_picked_file_mounts_or_selects`\n- `the_machine_and_post_load_buttons_are_live_in_the_browser` (AccessKit label, role `Button`, enabled state for \"Load machine (.mch)\", \"Load folder (.mch, .cps)\" and \"Load post (.cps)\"; no folder button on the desktop)\n\nOther tests:\n\n- `session_files::tests::a_bad_file_is_refused_by_name_and_never_kept` (app unit test; also pins the refusal by name for a project that names a file that is not loaded).\n- `setup_file_drop::tests::one_file_is_for_its_own_kind_in_any_case`.\n- Updated for the new law: `browser_files::tests::every_picker_and_folder_command_is_refused_by_name_in_the_browser`, `a_picker_the_browser_lacks_is_refused_by_name_not_ignored`, `a_file_button_is_greyed_with_its_reason_in_the_browser`.\n\nRed before the fix (reduced pins on unchanged `upstream/main`):\n\n- the drop pins failed with `drop refused: drop-2950-vmc.mch is not a model file (read: .stl, .obj, .step, .stp, .sc, .solidcraft)`;\n- the button pin failed with `LoadMachineDialog runs the browser's picker` / `left: Some(\"Not available in the browser yet: ...\")`.\n\nMutation checks (old code put back, pins run, code restored):\n\n- `crates/ui/src/browser_files.rs` from upstream: `the_machine_and_post_load_buttons_are_live_in_the_browser` red.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs` from upstream (drop route not called): the three drop pins red.\n- `crates/app/src/posting.rs` from upstream (no session read at post time): `a_dropped_cps_is_selected_and_posts_from_its_bytes` red.\n- `session_files::add_post` without its compile check: `several_dropped_files_land_and_each_bad_one_is_refused_by_name` red.\n- All pins green again after each restore.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` ran all 428 steps on the previous head. 427 passed. `ui suites: lib` failed in three machines-pane tests. The cause was a process-global store: the session machines of the new tests leaked into the machine list of tests on other threads.\n- The fix makes the store thread-local. The browser runs on one thread.\n- On the final head, `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --only \"app suites: lib\" --only \"ui suites: lib\"` is green (ui lib 1385 passed, 0 failed). Only `crates/app/src/session_files.rs` changed between the two heads, plus one test comment and the decision file. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The wasm32 build. The `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target is not installed on this machine, so the wasm-only code was not compiled. That code is: the folder input and batch read in `file_pick.rs`, the async drop read in `setup_file_drop.rs`, and the dialog openers in `state_picked.rs`. A reviewer with the target must run `cargo check -p camcraft-ui --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`.\n- A real browser. The tests use `State::browser_build` and in-memory drops as the stand-in.\n- Persistence in IndexedDB. Not built. The decision file lists the options for the maintainer.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3057 changes `file_drop::take_drop`. This PR does not change that function. It adds `setup_file_drop::take`, which `shell.rs` calls before `take_drop`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- Several open PRs touch `crates/app/src/posting.rs` and `crates/ui/src/state.rs` in other functions. This PR changes only `script_of`, `resolve_cps` (one line each), the `LoadMachineDialog` / `SelectPostDialog` arms and one new `CommandKind` variant.\n\n## MCP\n\nNo new MCP tool. The browser routes go through the existing `LoadMachineFile` and `SelectPostFile` commands, and the MCP machine and post tools read the session store through the same readers. `LoadSetupFolderDialog` is a browser-only picker. It changes no document state.\n\nDecision file: `docs/decisions/2950-browser-machine-post-files.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The browser build loads your own machine (.mch) and post (.cps) files from a picker, a folder picker or a drop; a bad file is refused by name.\n\nFixes #2950\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
